// t_61109061.  A function REACHED from the SELECTED ENTRY may not carry a
// RETURN semantic.  MEASURED against sce-cgc 475 - the C5122 diagnostic's own
// text ("semantics not allowed on functions other than the entry function") is
// WRONG about its rule: the reference accepts a parameter semantic on a called
// helper, and accepts full semantics on a function nothing calls.
//
// reached through a RETURN expression
// Compile with -e beta.  Reference verdict: REFUSE
float4 gamma(float4 t) : COLOR { return t*2.0; }
float4 beta(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return gamma(t); }
